	(text "MCU hooks: header J60 for an external SAMD51 board (DAC outputs, HV_MON for its ADC). No SAMD51 on Rev A."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 38.1 20.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "541dbba3-b519-4348-aecc-33a92914e91a")
	)
	(text "Design intent (Rev A, nothing here is simulated or measured)\n\nNo SAMD51 on Rev A. The header exposes the optional hooks only; the analog-first chain works without it (PROPOSED).\nSAMD51 DACs are 12-bit (decision-log standing correction); ADC inputs to be buffered later (UNRESOLVED).\nJ60 pin 1 (3V3) is a REFERENCE ONLY, 10 mA max: do not power an MCU board from it (PROPOSED).\nPull-downs R190-R192 (100k) hold DAC_GAIN, DAC_TH and DAC_HV at 0 V when no DAC is fitted (PROPOSED).\n  Pull-down polarity: UNRESOLVED. They may become pull-ups once the DAC polarity is decided.\nDAC_HV: 0 V vs Hi-Z is NOT the same set point (docs/calculations/apd-bias-design.md s.3.2 \"Range\", PROPOSED, hand calculation):\n  DAC alone spans +/-30.6 V (61 V span, LSB 14.9 mV); pot span 99 V; both at 0 V = 215 V hardware maximum (maximum trim);\n  both at 3.3 V = 55 V (firmware limit to >= 100 V). DAC pin Hi-Z at reset -> 135.9 V.\n  With R192 fitted and no DAC driving, DAC_HV reads 0 V -> the bias goes to the MAXIMUM end of the trim, not 135.9 V.\n  Check APD bias limits (100-220 V) before fitting any MCU board.\nHV_MON (~Vout/101) is the only HV observation point; keep it within the MCU ADC range with a buffer (UNRESOLVED)."
		(exclude_from_sim yes)
		(at 38.1 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a22ddc46-16eb-4407-a458-4dce4582cc77")
